            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_be5209a1">
               <titlePage label="Title on first music page (fol. 2v)" xml:id="titlePage_7a57118f">
                  <p xml:id="idm21">CONCERTO pro Clavicembal del Sigr. Vivaldi.</p>
               </titlePage>
               <titlePage label="First music page" xml:id="titlePage_b97fee06">
                  <p xml:id="idm23">at top left-hand corner added in ink: ‘20. no. 1.’ and the shelf mark ‘2668’ has been added in pencil, later cancelled in pencil.</p>
               </titlePage>
               <extent xml:id="extent_26af2588">1 bifolio</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_8f209251">42x27</dimensions>
               <watermark xml:id="watermark_ed79f61a">a visible emblem consisting of a crowned coat-of-arms with fleur-de-lis in the middle and 'CV' below the base, corresponding to paper found in J.S. Bach's 'Die Zeit, die Tag und Jahre macht' (1719; cf. Stinson:1990, 260). Paper of a dense quality; water-stained, and bifolio has markings of having been folded once.</watermark>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_69542c09">In 2<rend xml:id="idm28" rend="sup">o</rend>; upright format; music (fols. 2v, 1r, 1v, 2r); in all 1 bifolio. Hand-ruled paper, 18 staves (9 mm; single rastrum used) in dark brown ink and music in same ink. An autograph copy (Scheibe’s early handwriting) with additions and corrections in ink and should therefore be termed as a working copy. </physMedium>
            </physDesc>
